From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 01:02:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep xmlns:prefix declarations that the HTML parser left as
 attributes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

beta.5's svg_source writes the namespace of each element instead of copying
xmlns attributes, and drops every attribute whose name holds a colon. The HTML
parser keeps a prefixed element such as <html:link> under a literal local name,
and its xmlns:html declaration as a plain attribute. Without the declaration the
source is not well-formed XML, usvg rejects it, and the whole SVG paints nothing
(WPT svg/geometry and svg/shapes tests with html:link metadata).

Keep plain xmlns:<prefix> attributes. Skip xmlns:xlink, which the root already
declares.

beep-boop-🤖
---
 src/node/serialize.rs | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/node/serialize.rs b/src/node/serialize.rs
index 80d1063..596489a 100644
--- a/src/node/serialize.rs
+++ b/src/node/serialize.rs
@@ -87,6 +87,10 @@ fn write_xml_attr_name(
     let namespace = attr.namespace();
     match *namespace {
         ns!(xmlns) => return false,
+        // The HTML parser keeps `xmlns:html` as a plain attribute and prefixed element names
+        // as literal local names (`html:link`), which need that declaration to stay valid XML.
+        // The root already declares `xlink`.
+        ns!() if local.starts_with("xmlns:") && local.as_str() != "xmlns:xlink" => {}
         ns!() if local.contains(':') || local.as_str() == "xmlns" => return false,
         ns!() => {}
         ns!(xml) => writer.push_str("xml:"),
